** TODO =xsputn= loses its argument when it lies inside the buffer past =pbase ()=

=basic_stringbuf::xsputn= (=include/sstream.cc= 181-200) saves the
offset of an argument inside the put area before growing the buffer,
as ~__off = this->pbase () - __s~, and corrects =__s= after the growth
only when ~0 <= __off~. The offset is negative for every =__s= past
=pbase ()=, so such a call copies from the freed buffer. Only =__s ==
pbase ()= is corrected, the case STDCXX-576's program exercises. From
17d5eb29. Hypothesis, by reading, 2026-11-05.

Fix: ~__off = __s - this->pbase ()~.

Check: a =27.stringbuf.virtuals= row that grows the buffer with
~sputn (pbase () + 1, n)~ and compares the sequence.

