** TODO The configuration under =eccp= against GCC's

=config.h= under =eccp -A= differs from GCC's 11S beyond the other
entries of this chapter: no atomic built-ins, no =_RWSTD_THREAD= and
no TLS; =STD_TYPE_INFO= fails (the characterization declares its own
=type_info=; 12475dfe removed the =#pragma define_type_info= that
served =eccp=); =TYPE_INFO_DTOR= and =LIBC_EXCEPTION_SPEC= (#536,
an exception specification incompatible with glibc's) fail; the
special-member characterizations of the exception classes differ.
=STD_NOTHROW= fails to link: =libC.a= defines no =std::nothrow=
object. =long long= and extern templates are absent, which is
correct for C++03.

Without a feature macro glibc shows strict C++03 the ISO names only,
and the POSIX and XSI characterizations fail on an undefined
identifier: =DAYLIGHT=, =TIMEZONE=, =TM_GMTOFF=, =MADVISE=
(=caddr_t=), =THREAD_SAFE_EXCEPTIONS= (=pthread_setconcurrency=),
